event: response.output_text.done
data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","item_id":"msg_92c55744-f21f-9a71-bcda-b92945be5cac","output_index":4,"content_index":0,"text":"The latest stable Rust release is **1.99.1**, announced on October 15, 2026 by the Rust Release Team. The “latest” redirect (`https://blog.rust-lang.org/releases/latest`) points to that post. [web:0] [web:2]\n\n**1.99.1** is a point release that fixes regressions from earlier releases, including:\n- Missing `wcslen` symbol (link errors on some targets, especially UEFI with `std`)\n- Miscompilation of FFI `bool` return values on x86_64\n- `rust-lld` failing to load `libLLVM` on macOS when not invoked via the rustup proxy\n\nUpdate with `rustup update stable`. [web:0]\n\nThe previous stable feature release was **1.99.0** (October 1, 2026), which stabilized C-ABI variadic functions and clarified layout info from raw pointers. [web:1] The releases index lists 1.99.1 as the most recent announcement. [web:2]","logprobs":[],"sequence_number":252}

